WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.190
A bottle of hydrogen peroxide can sit
on a shelf for months, barely changing.

2
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.350
Pour some onto a slice of raw
potato, and it fizzes at once.

3
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.210
It's the same reaction, breaking
down to water and oxygen.

4
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:16.370
Months on the shelf,
seconds on the potato.

5
00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:21.210
So why does hydrogen peroxide fizz
at once on a slice of raw potato?

6
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:25.530
In this mission, you'll read energy profiles
and the Maxwell–Boltzmann distribution,

7
00:00:25.580 --> 00:00:29.090
and see what temperature
really does to a reaction.

8
00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:33.670
You'll also work out the energy barrier
for a reaction running in reverse.

9
00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:38.350
Your mission: explain why hydrogen
peroxide fizzes on the potato.
